Introduction
------------------------------------------------------------

persona is a lightweight hierarchical authorization library
for Clojure. It is currently a work in progress.

It checks whether a subject may perform a permission on a
resource, independently of authentication and identity
providers.


Installation
------------------------------------------------------------

This library can be installed from Clojars [1].


Authorization model
------------------------------------------------------------

- Namespaces isolate personas and assignments.
- Personas contain sets of permissions.
- Subjects identify users, groups, or service accounts.
- Assignments bind subjects to personas within a scope.
- The application supplies the resource's scope path,
  including its parents, for hierarchical authorization.

Personas and assignments can be changed at runtime. Storage
is backend-independent; an in-memory store is included.


Example
------------------------------------------------------------

  (require '[persona.core :as persona]
           '[persona.store.memory :as memory])

  (def store (memory/->memory-store))

  (persona/put-persona!
   store :acme
   {:id :editor
    :name "Editor"
    :permissions #{:document/read :document/write}})

  (persona/put-assignments!
   store :acme :editor
   [{:subject {:provider :ldap :id "team:editors"}
     :scope {:kind :project :id "website"}}])

  (persona/allowed?
   store :acme
   #{{:provider :ldap :id "team:editors"}}
   :document/write
   [{:kind :document :id "design.md"}
    {:kind :project :id "website"}])
  ;; => true

The project assignment grants access to the document through
the supplied parent scope.


